0..75 Comment "// The strings subject\'s shared declarations, imported by every source that"
76..154 Comment "// reads them (`import \"./string-base.gandr\" ;`): where a string\'s bytes live,"
155..234 Comment "// and the byte lists every claim reads and builds. A string is a value: a copy"
235..311 Comment "// is a new string, and no write to one is seen through another (Racordon et"
312..388 Comment "// al., \"Implementation strategies for mutable value semantics\", _Journal of"
389..460 Comment "// Object Technology_ 21(2), 2022, doi:10.5381/jot.2022.21.2.a2). Short"
461..539 Comment "// strings keep their bytes inline and long ones share a buffer until a write,"
540..595 Comment "// as the C++ and Rust small-string representations do."
597..632 Comment "// The lists the bytes are held in."
633..639 Keyword "import"
640..641 StringLit "\""
641..664 StringLit "../data/data-base.gandr"
664..665 StringLit "\""
666..667 Other ";"
